// @ARGS: --lib tests/lib
//
// @FR-F-Surface — `use lib::(name)` reaches what `lib::name` reaches and nothing more, and it
// refuses in the same words: an item `lib` declares without `pub` is "not `pub` in `lib`", and a
// name `lib` only imports for its own use names the library that owns it.  The import list said
// "Name 'hid_f' not found in library" for an item `privlib` does declare, which sends the reader
// looking for a missing item rather than a missing `pub`.  A name `lib` does not have at all
// keeps "not found" (tests/package_layout.rs `by_name_missing`).
// The qualified spelling's cells are in a-qualified-name-reaches-only-what-a-library-publishes.loft.
//
// @falsified-at: 23bc61e47 — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/3 -> 0/3 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/3 -> 0/3 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches)
// WITNESS: on main each of the three names is refused `Name '…' not found in library`.
// CHANNEL: the expected diagnostics.
// ARMED: nothing.
// HOLDS: every cell is a refusal, so only the message can move.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `hid_f` is not `pub` in `privlib`, so `use privlib::(hid_f)` cannot reach it
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `HID_C` is not `pub` in `privlib`, so `use privlib::(HID_C)` cannot reach it
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `use privlib::(c98_len)` reaches a name `privlib` only imports for its own use — it is `c98_math`'s
use privlib::(pub_f, hid_f, HID_C, c98_len);

fn main() {
  println("{pub_f()}");
}
